# NOTICE — Third-party models and libraries

AEGIS bundles or depends on the following third-party components. Each ships with its own licence;
nothing here is redistributed under the MIT licence in LICENSE.

## Models bundled in the extension package

Exactly these files, pinned by sha256 in `apps/extension/public/models/models.manifest.json`
(the release build refuses to complete if any differs):

| Model | Licence | Source | Used for |
|---|---|---|---|
| YuNet face detector (`face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx`) | MIT (Shiqi Yu) | [opencv/opencv_zoo](https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo/tree/main/models/face_detection_yunet) | Face detection |
| PP-OCRv5 mobile text detector and English / Devanagari recognizers, with their character dictionaries | Apache-2.0 (PaddleOCR; ONNX exports by RapidAI RapidOCR) | [RapidAI/RapidOCR v3.9.2](https://www.modelscope.cn/models/RapidAI/RapidOCR) | On-device text reading (OCR) |
| CLIP ViT-B/32 image encoder (`vit-vision.onnx`, int8-quantized) and precomputed text-prompt embeddings (`vit-prompts.bin`) | MIT (OpenAI CLIP weights, via open_clip_torch's `openai` tag) | [openai/CLIP](https://github.com/openai/CLIP), exported with `tools/models/` | Zero-shot screening of pictures and the screen-state label |

## Model used through an API, not bundled

| Model | Licence | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| Qwen3.8-27B (`qwen/qwen3.8-27b`), hosted by Groq | as published by its authors | Planning each step, from the redacted context. Called from the extension with the user's own Groq API key (bring your own key); subject to Groq's terms |

## Development-only components (not in a release)

- OpenAI Privacy Filter (profile L NER, ~950 MB): fetched separately for browser tests; never part of a release build.
- FastAPI, Pydantic and vLLM (MIT, MIT, Apache-2.0): the legacy server gateway and its self-hosted model option, used by the evaluation harness and dev runs only.

## Key libraries in the extension

| Library | Licence | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| ONNX Runtime Web (JS and the WebAssembly binary in the package) | MIT | On-device inference (WebGPU / WASM) |
| Preact | MIT | Panel UI |
| WXT | MIT | Cross-browser extension build |
| Ajv (generated validators) | MIT | Validating protocol messages |

Full dependency licences are also available via each package's own `package.json` /
`pyproject.toml` and the resolved lockfiles (`pnpm-lock.yaml`, `uv.lock`).
